**Proposition 9.2 (boundary witnesses).** The following exact witnesses
distinguish the relevant claims.

1. The five-row reader with $d=0$ performs its one zero test and no payload
   IN. For $d\ge1$, local cuts 1 and 2 are respectively before and after
   its first IN. They differ even when its later completed frame is the
   same. The next cut additionally executes WR.
2. In a capacity-one accepted $\rho\alpha=\beta$ write, packets 01 and 10
   differ in both bits. After the first changed bit the intermediate
   packet is 11 or 00, depending on write order. Neither is a valid
   complete one-token source packet.
3. Fix a cover with bound $b$ and request $k>b$. Later request processing
   may advance actual receipts beyond $k$. Correct comparison to the
   frozen $b$ still rejects $k$.
4. If a package instead stores a pointer to mutable latest-cover, replacing
